{
  "borough": "Waltham Forest",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development is unacceptable in principle,\r\nwhereby the proposed subdivision of commercial space for residential development\r\nat ground floor level fails to contribute&nbsp;to the vitality and viability of\r\nthe District Town Centre contrary to Policy(s) and 40 and 41 of the Waltham\r\nForest adopted Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).",
    "The proposed and altered residential unit(s), due to their\r\npoor layout creates a cramped form of living environment, failing to meet\r\nminimum space standards as well as failing to achieve good quality housing for\r\nfuture occupants contrary to Policy(s) 53 and 56&nbsp;of the Waltham Forest\r\nadopted Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).",
    "Due to insufficient information in relation to the Outline\r\nConstruction Logistic Plan as submitted, an adequate assessment could not be\r\nmade in relation to how the proposed development would be built or serviced\r\nwithout severely affecting the public highway contrary to Policy 65&nbsp;of the\r\nWaltham Forest adopted Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).",
    "Due to insufficient information in relation to the location\r\nof internal or external refuse storage, an adequate assessment could not be\r\nmade whether adequate facilities for the storage of refuse and recycling have\r\nbeen provided for the proposed residential unit contrary to Policy 57&nbsp;of\r\nthe Waltham Forest adopted Local Plan Pt 1 (2024).",
    "The applicant has failed to enter into a S106 agreement and\r\ntherefore not in compliance with Policy 94&nbsp;of the Waltham Forest adopted\r\nLocal Plan Pt 1 (2024), specifically in relation to the following planning\r\nobligations requirements (figures applicable at the time of the assessment of\r\nthe application).&nbsp;Car Free Development - the development is to be classified\r\nas car-free and residents will not be eligible for parking permits.A Condition survey of the carriageway and footways fronting\r\nthe site prior to the commencement of any worksFinancial contribution of £1,000.00 toward improving\r\nsustainable modes of transport including walking and cycling in the sites\r\nvicinity which will directly benefit new residents in this developmentFinancial contribution of £627.00 towards the Epping Forest\r\nSAMMFinancial contribution of £250.00 would be requested towards\r\nmonitoring of the Construction Logistics Plan.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFinancial contribution of 5% of&nbsp;s106 monitoring fees"
  ],
